          "source": "palm",
          "verdict": "malicious",
          "category": "code_insight",
          "analysis": "This is a MIPS variant of the Mozi P2P botnet. It spreads by exploiting known vulnerabilities in IoT devices, evidenced by strings related to HNAP, SOAP, and various router exploits (e.g., HuaweiHomeGateway, GponForm). It downloads and executes additional payloads, as shown by URLs ending in `Mozi.m`, `Mozi.a`, etc. The malware modifies `iptables` to allow its C2 traffic and attempts to gain persistence by writing to startup locations like `/etc/rc.local` and `/etc/init.d/S95baby.sh`.",
          "id": "f7375f0ae0287b6aa966ae8ade9cadbd13821544a242f8418554ec462b71f8fd-file-palm"
